                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "petiole",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fba83ce6-faf5-303d-906e-1ed6be97f530",
                                        "entry_id": "3955d715-30d1-3566-8984-6af87c3eb2ce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The stalk of a leaf, attaching the blade to the stem."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b826f04-e29c-41e0-8266-aab98b83f83f",
                                                "sense_id": "fba83ce6-faf5-303d-906e-1ed6be97f530",
                                                "text": "Most insects consume tissue from the leaf blade were measured just past the twist on the side away only, leaving the leaf petioles unscathed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7e88fd8-7dcf-4eb4-9265-9b6e27ab80d7",
                                                "sense_id": "fba83ce6-faf5-303d-906e-1ed6be97f530",
                                                "text": "By contrast, the petioles of large pinnate leaves, as well as stems, typically resist torsion by placing stiff materials with high elastic moduli (like sclerenchyma) toward the perimeters of their cross sections."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eeaa8590-d081-4714-816f-dbeaf21e06d8",
                                                "sense_id": "fba83ce6-faf5-303d-906e-1ed6be97f530",
                                                "text": "An example of this is leaf petioles. Some species of trees have pinnate leaves which, when the leaves fall, shed pinnae from the petiole, which is then left as a tapering, somewhat flexible rod."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a2ee98b-32d9-33f1-8c42-70d8a87fa550",
                                        "entry_id": "3955d715-30d1-3566-8984-6af87c3eb2ce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A narrow or constricted segment of the body of an insect; especially, the metasomal segment of certain Hymenoptera, such as wasps."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee91132e-51e0-3d17-84a9-eae23d3cccec",
                                        "entry_id": "3955d715-30d1-3566-8984-6af87c3eb2ce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The stalk at the base of the nest of the paper wasp."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f67afb92-1de2-4feb-a965-9fd1df70ac4d",
                        "source_entry_id": "85ed9a89-a5b9-39b7-80cd-920b6ebcdb6a",
                        "source_sense_id": "871c5349-e817-38b6-83c1-c5f0f16394b8",
                        "target_lang_word": "pétiole",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pétiole",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3cc4641b-87a6-37d9-b1e1-bd751c26b04e",
                                        "entry_id": "7f765475-96c4-34d7-a0fe-b7152e3df346",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Partie rétrécie de certaines feuilles unissant le limbe à la tige."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92b379f7-a117-4aea-a68f-50efe9643111",
                                                "sense_id": "3cc4641b-87a6-37d9-b1e1-bd751c26b04e",
                                                "text": "Jusqu'à présent, ils n'en tirent aucun profit. Le jatrophe est classé dans l'ordre des Renonculinées, famille des Euphorbiacées, tribu des Crotonées. La feuille, caduque, simple palmatilobée, comprend 5 grands lobes et un pétiole de 0 m. 30 à 0 m. 40 de longueur."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cea1029a-c0d1-3493-af10-ca7fe35265e6",
                                        "entry_id": "7f765475-96c4-34d7-a0fe-b7152e3df346",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chez les hyménoptères apocrites comme les guêpes et les fourmis, deuxième segment de l'abdomen fortement rétréci. Il peut être simple, double ou en forme d'écaille."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d3623af-d68a-4cd1-87c2-4f2aa5184523",
                                                "sense_id": "cea1029a-c0d1-3493-af10-ca7fe35265e6",
                                                "text": "Un des deux mâles saisit son adversaire au niveau du cou ou du pétiole et le soulève pour le priver d'appui. Cette prise peut durer plusieurs heures et se termine par la mort du plus faible."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5bad775-39cd-3567-867a-6c37ffb60dd9",
                                        "entry_id": "7f765475-96c4-34d7-a0fe-b7152e3df346",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tige de suspension des nids de guêpes et de frelons."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
